{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgArwW7oRjJFzEHx7qk9Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The server has the problem: four of the ten checks fail, and C6 is a WARN, which counts as a fail. The full report is in `ANSWER.md` in this folder. I did not change `server.py`.\n\n**Checks that fail**\n- **C2, refusals as protocol errors:** a note that doesn't exist, or a missing `id`, returns JSON-RPC `-32602`. It should be a result with `isError: true`.\n- **C5, serialisation:** two calls with wrong-typed arguments return an empty body, which does not parse as JSON.\n- **C7, logging:** each call gets one log line, but the two crashing calls get none.\n- **C10, output schemas:** `search_notes` declares `{\"type\": \"object\"}`, which accepts `{}` as a wrong answer.\n- **C6, version:** there is no surface lock in the repo. I did not compare against the MCP Registry because that is an external service.\n\n**Checks that pass:** C1 (tool list works without a token), C3 (session survives an error), C4 (valid results match their schema), C8 (names are clean), C9 (version negotiation is honest).\n\n**Most serious findings outside the ten checks**\n1. **Resources are advertised but refused.** `initialize` advertises resources, but anonymous `resources/list` returns HTTP 401. A client can mark the whole server as needing auth, even though the tool list is open.\n2. **Crash on `null` or a wrong type.** `search_notes` with `\"limit\": null` and `get_note` with `\"id\": []` both return no response at all. The server stays up, but the client gets no error and the model cannot correct itself.\n\nThe other findings in `ANSWER.md` are lower priority: notifications get an error reply, `Origin` is not checked, `dev-token-123` is a write token whenever `NOTES_TOKEN` is unset, and two argument limits are not enforced.\n\n**How I tested:** I ran the server locally, then stopped it. I only sent read-only calls. I did not call `add_note`, which is a write tool. I did not record anything on worklore.dev or any other external service."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":56097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":444},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c79d121-a94c-48f8-8dbe-0f27cca83a12","uuid":"5499f3f2-80db-4a51-9c5d-045d0dfc0223","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:10:11.256Z","request_id":"req_011CgArwVsfJWBnyZ99ztxHP"}
